//! D299/D304 — pyramid H¹ **field assembly** vs MFEM 4.10 ground truth.
//!
//! Round 43 (D191) fixed `DofManager::build_pyramid_pk` to number pyramid H¹
//! field DOFs in MFEM's entity order, but the *reference element* the
//! assembler paired with that numbering was still the layer-ordered
//! equispaced [`PyramidPk`]: from p = 2 on, slot s of `element_dofs` was
//! multiplied by the shape function of a *different* node ("layer-order
//! basis × entity-order `dofs_flat`").
//!
//! The fix has two halves, both 1:1 ports of MFEM 4.10's
//! `H1_BergotPyramidElement` (`fem/fe/fe_h1.cpp`, the `pyr_type=0` pyramid
//! that `H1_FECollection(p, 3, GaussLobatto)` puts on pyramid cells — the
//! family fem-rs numbers pyramid H¹ spaces with):
//!
//! 1. `fem_element::H1PyramidPk` — the Bergot element in entity slot order at
//!    the GLL-barycentric nodes (part (b): p ≥ 3 positions leave the
//!    equispaced lattice);
//! 2. the pyramid arms of `assembler::ref_elem_vol_h1`, `mixed::ref_elem_vol`
//!    and `bbar::ref_elem_vol` wired to it (part (c)).
//!
//! Ground truth: `tmp/d304/pyr_mass_probe.cpp` (run in WSL against
//! `$HOME/mfem410_ser`, results in `tmp/d304/cpp_mass_p{2,3,4}.txt`).  It
//! computes MFEM's element mass matrix on the single straight unit pyramid
//! with a collapsed tensor Gauss rule exact for the integrand (total sums
//! verified = volume = 1/3), and prints it in the space's *slot* order
//! (slot → internal dof resolved by node-position matching).  On the unit
//! pyramid fem-rs' global numbering equals the slot order, so the assembled
//! mass matrix must equal the dump entry for entry.

use fem_assembly::{Assembler, BilinearIntegrator, QpData};
use fem_element::quadrature::gauss_jacobi;
use fem_element::{H1PyramidPk, QuadratureRule, ReferenceElement};
use fem_mesh::{element_type::ElementType, Mesh};
use fem_space::{FESpace, H1Space};
use nalgebra::{DMatrix, DVector};


